## Step 4 – Setup package repository and shared to client servers using sftp
---
Configured sftp server to share rhel system packages to client servers and in client servers configured sftp ip in /etc/yum.repos.d

## Step 5 – Configure Storage

Configured the attached storage using LVM.

```bash
pvcreate /dev/sdb

vgcreate rhel /dev/sdb

lvcreate -L 30G -n apps rhel

lvcreate -L 40G -n loggers rhel
```

Created XFS filesystems.

```bash
mkfs.xfs /dev/rhel/apps
mkfs.xfs /dev/rhel/loggers
```

Created mount points.

```bash
mkdir -p /apps
mkdir -p /loggers
```

Mounted the filesystems.

```bash
mount /dev/rhel/apps /apps
mount /dev/rhel/loggers /loggers
```

Configured persistent mounts.

```bash
echo "UUID=$(blkid -s UUID -o value /dev/rhel/apps) /apps xfs defaults 0 0" >> /etc/fstab
echo "UUID=$(blkid -s UUID -o value /dev/rhel/loggers) /loggers xfs defaults 0 0" >> /etc/fstab

mount -a
```

---

## Step 6 – Create Application Users

Created the required application users.

* app1
* app2
* app3

Automated user creation using Bash.

```bash
#!/bin/bash

USERS=("app1 "app2" "app3)
PASSWORD="Password@123"

for user in "${USERS[@]}"
do
    id "$user" &>/dev/null || useradd -m "$user"

    echo "$PASSWORD" | passwd --stdin "$user"

    chage -d 0 "$user"
    id $user

done
```

Verified user accounts.

